<hr>
<h3>Part 5: Teach-Back Unlock</h3>
<div class="question">17. (Multiple Choice) You don't truly "own" an idea until you can:</div>
<ul>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Copy it exactly from the textbook.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Explain it in your own words.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Get an AI to write it for you.</li>
<li><span class="checkbox">&#9744;</span> Highlight it in three different colors.</li>
</ul>
<div class="question">18. (Scenario) You write a 5-sentence explanation of a science concept in your own words. You ask the AI to score your "teach-back." The AI gives you a 3/5 because you copied a sentence directly from its previous hint. What should you do next?</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="question">19. (Classification) Which of these is a stronger teach-back?</div>
<p>A) "Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants and some other organisms use sunlight to synthesize foods from carbon dioxide and water."</p>
<p>B) "Photosynthesis is basically how plants make their own food. They use sunlight, water, and air to cook up energy so they can grow."</p>
<p>Explain your choice.</p>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
  <p class="response-placeholder">[ Type your conceptual answer or explanation here... ]</p>
</div>
<div class="response-box">
  <p class="response-label">✍️ Student Response Area (Double-click to type)</p>
